stage_b_reviewed_content.statement:
Let $X$ be a scheme. The following are equivalent
\begin{enumerate}
\item $X$ is quasi-excellent, and
\item $X$ is a G-scheme and J-2.
\end{enumerate}

conclusions:
The following are equivalent
\begin{enumerate}
\item $X$ is quasi-excellent, and
\item $X$ is a G-scheme and J-2.
\end{enumerate}

stage_b_reviewed_content.statement:
Let $X$ be a scheme. The following are equivalent
\begin{enumerate}
\item $X$ is excellent, and
\item $X$ is quasi-excellent and universally catenary.
\end{enumerate}

conclusions:
The following are equivalent
\begin{enumerate}
\item $X$ is excellent, and
\item $X$ is quasi-excellent and universally catenary.
\end{enumerate}
